<title>SWEDEN: Second shift for Saab Auto gearbox unit.</title>
<headline>Second shift for Saab Auto gearbox unit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saab Automobile's gearbox shop in Gothenburg is introducing a second daily shift from today, company newspaper Saab Idag reported.</p>
<p>Production will rise to 450 gearboxes a day from 380.</p>
<p>Demand from both Saab and Opel has increased, especially for the Opel Sintra.</p>
<p>The Gothenburg factory sends gearboxes for the Sintra to Atlanta, Georgia where the car is built, manager Nils Tjader told the newspaper.</p>
<p>-- Henrik Alberius, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1250</p>
</text>
